WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.408 --> 00:00:03.078
- She's a British novelist
best known as the author

00:00:03.078 --> 00:00:05.536
of the Harry Potter fantasy series.

00:00:05.536 --> 00:00:07.653
The books have gained
world wide attention,

00:00:07.653 --> 00:00:12.163
won multiple awards and have
sold over 400 million copies.

00:00:12.163 --> 00:00:15.513
In 2004, Forbes named her the first person

00:00:15.513 --> 00:00:18.600
to become a billionaire by writing books.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.767
She's JK Rowling and here are
her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:27.458
- Failure gave me an inner
security that I had never

00:00:27.458 --> 00:00:30.139
attained by passing examinations.

00:00:30.139 --> 00:00:32.358
Failure taught me things
about myself that I could

00:00:32.358 --> 00:00:34.541
have learned no other way.

00:00:34.541 --> 00:00:37.115
I discovered that I had a strong will

00:00:37.115 --> 00:00:40.036
and more discipline than I had suspected.

00:00:40.036 --> 00:00:43.463
I also found out that I
had friends whose value

00:00:43.463 --> 00:00:47.040
was truly above the price of rubies.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.575
The knowledge that you have
emerged wiser and stronger

00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:52.735
from setbacks means that
you are, ever after,

00:00:52.735 --> 00:00:56.108
secure in your ability to survive.

00:00:56.108 --> 00:00:58.996
You will never truly know
yourself or the strength

00:00:58.996 --> 00:01:01.982
of your relationships,
until both have been tested

00:01:01.982 --> 00:01:03.822
by adversity.

00:01:03.822 --> 00:01:06.953
Such knowledge is a true gift,

00:01:06.953 --> 00:01:09.578
for all that it is painfully won

00:01:09.578 --> 00:01:12.174
and it has been worth more
than any qualification

00:01:12.174 --> 00:01:14.120
I ever earned.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.478
I was on the train from
Manchester to London

00:01:16.478 --> 00:01:18.526
and it came, just came.

00:01:18.526 --> 00:01:21.204
- Had something like that
ever happened to you before?

00:01:21.204 --> 00:01:22.818
- Yes, truthfully.

00:01:22.818 --> 00:01:25.089
I mean, other ideas have just come to me,

00:01:25.089 --> 00:01:27.131
because I think, if you're a writer

00:01:27.131 --> 00:01:30.040
and that's what you spend a
huge amount of time doing,

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.574
ideas do come to you.

00:01:31.574 --> 00:01:35.157
But nothing had ever
come, so, with such a,

00:01:36.867 --> 00:01:39.515
I felt God, I'd love to write that.

00:01:39.515 --> 00:01:41.674
When I got off the train,
I went straight home

00:01:41.674 --> 00:01:42.896
and I started writing.

00:01:42.896 --> 00:01:45.119
It is one of the amazing
and wonderful things

00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:48.198
about literature as
about film and music is,

00:01:48.198 --> 00:01:50.169
it's utterly subjective.

00:01:50.169 --> 00:01:52.356
- [Interviewer] It's somebodies opinion.

00:01:52.356 --> 00:01:54.594
- That's the point of it,
you know, that's the point.

00:01:54.594 --> 00:01:56.313
Of course, you move in that world.

00:01:56.313 --> 00:01:58.399
If you expect to just stand under a shower

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:00.292
of perpetual praise, there's
something wrong with you.

00:02:00.292 --> 00:02:01.421
- [Interviewer] That's exactly right.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.711
- You will get criticism.

00:02:02.711 --> 00:02:04.587
I knew that going in
and the funny thing is,

00:02:04.587 --> 00:02:06.504
I'm not a particularly,

00:02:07.343 --> 00:02:09.534
I was never a very confident person

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:10.929
and there are areas in my life

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:12.913
in which I'm very thin-skinned.

00:02:12.913 --> 00:02:14.082
But not in this area.

00:02:14.082 --> 00:02:16.957
In this area, I think
it's right and proper

00:02:16.957 --> 00:02:19.300
I should be criticized
and that's literature.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.714
- [Interviewer] And can you learn--

00:02:20.714 --> 00:02:22.282
- [Interviewer] Did you write in here?

00:02:22.282 --> 00:02:26.363
- Mm hmm, this is really
the room where I finished

00:02:26.363 --> 00:02:28.696
Philosopher's Stone in here.

00:02:31.095 --> 00:02:35.260
This is really where I turned
my life around, completely.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:39.010
I mean, my life changed
so much in this fact.

00:02:45.996 --> 00:02:48.575
I feel I really became myself here.

00:02:48.575 --> 00:02:49.787
And that everything stripped away.

00:02:49.787 --> 00:02:54.058
I've made such a mess of
things, but that was freeing.

00:02:54.058 --> 00:02:57.077
So I want to write, so I write
the book, I wrote the book.

00:02:57.077 --> 00:02:58.818
What is the worst that can happen?

00:02:58.818 --> 00:03:00.225
It gets turned down by
every publisher in Britain,

00:03:00.225 --> 00:03:01.058
big deal.

00:03:02.616 --> 00:03:06.783
So you know, it's really
back to the wool time here.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.144
The bedrooms are not, well, my bedroom,

00:03:11.144 --> 00:03:12.978
the bedroom is a lot tidier now.

00:03:12.978 --> 00:03:13.811
God.

00:03:17.727 --> 00:03:19.227
God, that's much--

00:03:20.137 --> 00:03:23.304
The place was a tip when I lived here.

00:03:24.357 --> 00:03:27.366
Oh, there are Harry Potter books.

00:03:27.366 --> 00:03:29.533
Now that is really freaky.

00:03:34.248 --> 00:03:37.017
And for years now I felt
like, if it all disappeared,

00:03:37.017 --> 00:03:40.850
and some days I do feel
like that, is it real?

00:03:42.612 --> 00:03:44.196
Then this is where I would
come back to, you know.

00:03:44.196 --> 00:03:45.459
This would be my baseline.

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:47.209
I'd be back in Neath.

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:50.834
Obviously if I'd known that,

00:03:51.904 --> 00:03:53.053
well was it 10 years,

00:03:53.053 --> 00:03:56.734
yeah, 10 years on, I'd come
back here with a film crew

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.647
and there would be my published
books in someone else's

00:03:59.647 --> 00:04:01.771
bookcase in this room.

00:04:01.771 --> 00:04:04.854
I mean, it's really incredible to me.

00:04:06.211 --> 00:04:07.461
Really, I mean,

00:04:09.084 --> 00:04:09.917
yes.

00:04:15.971 --> 00:04:19.028
Because it's such a well
worn part of my story now,

00:04:19.028 --> 00:04:22.111
its a big yawn to here how I wrote it

00:04:23.737 --> 00:04:25.207
as though it was all some sort

00:04:25.207 --> 00:04:27.541
of publicity stunt I did for a year.

00:04:27.541 --> 00:04:30.874
But it was my life and it was very hard.

00:04:32.586 --> 00:04:34.243
I didn't know there was going to be

00:04:34.243 --> 00:04:36.493
this fairy tale resolution.

00:04:38.813 --> 00:04:42.168
Coming back here is just full of ghosts.

00:04:42.168 --> 00:04:44.918
I remember once, and it was like,

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:48.640
well, like I'm going to call
it a flash of clairvoyance.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.915
Now, obviously, if it hadn't come true,

00:04:49.915 --> 00:04:52.372
it would just be some round
and crazy thought I'd had,

00:04:52.372 --> 00:04:55.129
but I do remember one day,
writing Philosopher's Stone.

00:04:55.129 --> 00:04:57.958
I was walking away from the
cafe where I'd been working.

00:04:57.958 --> 00:04:59.698
- Philosopher's Stone which
became Sorcerer's Stone.

00:04:59.698 --> 00:05:00.875
- Which became Sorcerer's Stone, exactly.

00:05:00.875 --> 00:05:02.716
So that's the first novel.

00:05:02.716 --> 00:05:05.735
I had this moment where
I suddenly thought,

00:05:05.735 --> 00:05:07.422
it was like another voice speaking to me.

00:05:07.422 --> 00:05:09.427
The voice said, "the
difficult thing's going

00:05:09.427 --> 00:05:10.625
to be to get published."

00:05:10.625 --> 00:05:13.399
"If it's published, it will be huge."

00:05:13.399 --> 00:05:14.232
- [Oprah] Wow.

00:05:14.232 --> 00:05:15.520
- And that is exactly what it was.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:20.458
- So there was some hint that
the voice had said to you.

00:05:20.458 --> 00:05:21.757
- [JK Rowling] Well the thing
is, you've got to believe,

00:05:21.757 --> 00:05:22.590
haven't you?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.423
- Yes.

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:27.379
- You know, I was not the
world's most secure person.

00:05:27.379 --> 00:05:29.502
I wasn't someone with an enormous amount,

00:05:29.502 --> 00:05:32.048
in fact, I'd say I was someone
with not much self belief

00:05:32.048 --> 00:05:35.998
at all and yet in this one
thing in my life, I believed.

00:05:35.998 --> 00:05:37.698
That was the one thing in my life, I felt,

00:05:37.698 --> 00:05:39.463
I can tell a story.

00:05:39.463 --> 00:05:40.489
There's always trepidation.

00:05:40.489 --> 00:05:42.664
I think that people might
be surprised to know

00:05:42.664 --> 00:05:45.557
that I felt trepidation every
time I produced a Potter book.

00:05:45.557 --> 00:05:48.484
You know, the weight of
expectation there was,

00:05:48.484 --> 00:05:49.594
I won't say crushing.

00:05:49.594 --> 00:05:51.732
It was extraordinary and
wonderful to have that weight

00:05:51.732 --> 00:05:52.565
of expectation.

00:05:52.565 --> 00:05:53.398
But at times--

00:05:53.398 --> 00:05:55.035
- [Interviewer] You were
competing with yourself?

00:05:55.035 --> 00:05:57.842
Yeah and with the expectations,
a lattaly of millions

00:05:57.842 --> 00:06:00.280
of fans, all of whom were
very invested in the story

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.666
and wanted to see what they wanted to see,

00:06:02.666 --> 00:06:03.809
and I knew where I was going.

00:06:03.809 --> 00:06:06.611
I had to put on mental
blinkers a lot and just think,

00:06:06.611 --> 00:06:07.444
I know where I'm going.

00:06:07.444 --> 00:06:09.742
I must not be influenced by this.

00:06:09.742 --> 00:06:13.223
Given a time turner, I would
tell my 21 year old self

00:06:13.223 --> 00:06:15.822
that personal happiness
lies in knowing that life

00:06:15.822 --> 00:06:20.086
is not a checklist of
acquisition or achievement.

00:06:20.086 --> 00:06:24.209
Your qualifications, your
CV, are not your life,

00:06:24.209 --> 00:06:26.897
though you will meet many
people of my age and older

00:06:26.897 --> 00:06:29.065
who confuse the two.

00:06:29.065 --> 00:06:32.837
Life is difficult and
complicated and beyond anyone's

00:06:32.837 --> 00:06:36.533
total control and the
humility to know that

00:06:36.533 --> 00:06:39.981
will enable you to
survive its vicissitudes.

00:06:39.981 --> 00:06:44.034
I often get asked by younger
readers what I would advise

00:06:44.034 --> 00:06:46.087
if you want to be a writer.

00:06:46.087 --> 00:06:48.228
This is the way I did it,
so that's the only advice

00:06:48.228 --> 00:06:49.769
I can give.

00:06:49.769 --> 00:06:52.359
You've got to read as
much as you possibly can,

00:06:52.359 --> 00:06:55.002
'cause that's the best way
to recognize good writing

00:06:55.002 --> 00:06:56.580
and to learn what makes bad writing,

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.807
and those are very good things.

00:06:58.807 --> 00:07:00.784
You'll probably go through
a phase where you imitate

00:07:00.784 --> 00:07:01.780
your favorite writers.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:02.613
That's perfectly okay.

00:07:02.613 --> 00:07:04.417
That's another learning process.

00:07:04.417 --> 00:07:08.318
You resign yourself to writing
lots and lots of rubbish.

00:07:08.318 --> 00:07:10.046
You've just got to write
that out of your system

00:07:10.046 --> 00:07:12.972
and sooner or later,
you'll hit what you really

00:07:12.972 --> 00:07:16.691
should be doing and what is your genre.

00:07:16.691 --> 00:07:17.855
And perseverance.

00:07:17.855 --> 00:07:21.517
You've got to persevere,
'cause it is a career

00:07:21.517 --> 00:07:24.326
with a lot of knock-backs,
but the rewards are huge.

00:07:24.326 --> 00:07:27.885
I don't mean, in the sense
that if that's what you really

00:07:27.885 --> 00:07:29.832
want to do, to be able to do it lifelong

00:07:29.832 --> 00:07:32.523
is the best thing in the world.

00:07:32.523 --> 00:07:34.318
Very rewarding.

00:07:34.318 --> 00:07:35.151
But it's not a career for people
who are easily discouraged,

00:07:35.151 --> 00:07:36.484
that's for sure.

00:07:37.842 --> 00:07:39.259
To their parents,

00:07:41.431 --> 00:07:43.727
don't tell them its unrealistic.

00:07:43.727 --> 00:07:45.213
Never say that.

00:07:45.213 --> 00:07:46.930
Because even if they're
not published, writing,

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:49.160
well, writing is the
passion of my life, so,

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.576
it's an important thing to do.

00:07:51.576 --> 00:07:54.189
I've always, always, always
wanted to be a writer.

00:07:54.189 --> 00:07:55.986
Obviously you want to be a writer.

00:07:55.986 --> 00:07:57.971
You want to, you dream
of supporting yourself

00:07:57.971 --> 00:08:00.811
through writing, definitely.

00:08:00.811 --> 00:08:03.536
But it is a bit of both
because I was very much aware

00:08:03.536 --> 00:08:06.853
that children's books, the
possibility of supporting

00:08:06.853 --> 00:08:09.360
yourself solely by writing
children's books is slim.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:12.572
That's the reality of it, which
I was fully aware of that.

00:08:12.572 --> 00:08:16.878
In that sense, this has all
come as a huge, enormous shock.

00:08:16.878 --> 00:08:19.594
I'm delighted, because
I always wanted to write

00:08:19.594 --> 00:08:22.322
and always have written,
but my realistic side

00:08:22.322 --> 00:08:25.816
had not allowed me to dream
of half of what's happened

00:08:25.816 --> 00:08:27.005
to me, truthfully.

00:08:27.005 --> 00:08:29.804
If you choose to use
your status and influence

00:08:29.804 --> 00:08:32.604
to raise your voice on behalf
of those who have no voice,

00:08:32.604 --> 00:08:36.656
if you choose to identify,
not only with the powerful,

00:08:36.656 --> 00:08:39.905
but with the powerless,
if you retain the ability

00:08:39.905 --> 00:08:42.664
to imagine yourself into the
lives of those who do not

00:08:42.664 --> 00:08:45.324
have your advantages,
then it will not only

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:48.824
be your proud families who
celebrate your existence,

00:08:48.824 --> 00:08:51.875
but thousands and millions
of people whose reality

00:08:51.875 --> 00:08:54.478
you have helped change.

00:08:54.478 --> 00:08:57.868
We do not need magic
to transform our world.

00:08:57.868 --> 00:09:01.341
We carry all the power we
need inside ourselves already.

00:09:01.341 --> 00:09:04.100
We have the power to imagine better.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.689
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:05.689 --> 00:09:08.827
I made this video because
Natasha asked me to,

00:09:08.827 --> 00:09:10.840
so if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.899
to profile next, leave
it in the comments below

00:09:12.899 --> 00:09:14.570
and we'll see what I can do.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.532
I'd also love to know which
of JK Rowling's top 10 tips

00:09:17.532 --> 00:09:19.227
meant the most to you.

00:09:19.227 --> 00:09:20.273
Leave it in the comments.

00:09:20.273 --> 00:09:21.822
We're going to join in the discussion.

00:09:21.822 --> 00:09:23.056
Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:23.056 --> 00:09:24.015
Have a great day.

00:09:24.015 --> 00:09:27.682
Continue to Believe
and we'll see you soon.

